      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree, I've come to this feedback hub to check if someone had the same issue. I think this is too much, before we were just having 2 layers for a heart emoji for example. Now it's 4.\n\nAnd me too, I spend too much time to find the emoji I want in a middle of a conversation.\n\nI agree for \"favorite\" list, or at least \"recent\". And I agree for the stickers and emoji separated from one \"emoji and stickers\" submenu istead to reduce a layer.\n\nAnother solution I suggest is featuring the possibility to use OSC to trigger an emoji so we can use a third party app to trigger the emoji we want (soundboard, voicecommand...)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-07-10T18:31:34.548Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I actually use a few of the default emoji still, but with the new changes they are so many menus deep. It takes me like 10 seconds to get there sometimes.  I'd like to be able to add the few that I use to the inventory managed menus.\n\nI also think emoji and sticker menus could potentially be moved up a layer as it's very hard to quickly use them, especially in VR where some sticks may not be so accurate and reliable.\n\nA second potential solution would be a \"favourites\" emoji and/or sticker menu on the top level of the EM which allows adding any custom or default emoji and/or sticker to it.\n\nJust a few thoughts as a mute who likes to occasionally be able to quickly access an emoji to react to something.",
